<title>USA: Livestock/meat crossings at U.S./Canadian border.</title>
<headline>Livestock/meat crossings at U.S./Canadian border.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agriculture Canada reported the following preliminary livestock and meat crossings at the U.S./Canadian border. - USDA</p>
<p>Canadian Imports from the U.S.:		    yr to   yr ago</p>
<p>			03/15/97 03/08/97 03/16/96   date    to date</p>
<p>Livestock/in head</p>
<p>Slaughter Steers:    101	139	4 :     720	 789</p>
<p>Heifers:		   6	 81	3 :     358	 176</p>
<p>Cows:		    751	698    432 :   8,552     4,739</p>
<p>Bulls:		    33	 29	9 :     425	 100</p>
<p>Totals:		  891	947    448 :  10,055     5,804</p>
<p>Canadian Imports from the U.S. - Meat (1,000 lbs):</p>
<p>     PERIOD    PREVIOUS    LAST     1997	SAME     YTD</p>
<p>     ENDING    WEEK	  YEAR    YEAR TO   PERIOD   PERCENT</p>
<p>     03/15/97  03/08/97  03/16/96   Date*    Last yr.  Change</p>
<p>Beef  4,065     4,482     3,737 :  42,405    45,163  -   6.1%</p>
<p>Pork  2,196     1,603     1,539 :  16,440    16,748  -   1.8%</p>
